<RuleHeader />

### What it does

Enforces getter/setter pairs in objects and classes.

### Why is this bad?

It's a common mistake in JavaScript to create an object with just a setter
for a property but never have a corresponding getter defined for it.
Without a getter, you cannot read the property, so it ends up not being used.

### Examples

Examples of **incorrect** code for this rule:

```js
var o = {
  set a(value) {
    this.val = value;
  },
};

class C {
  set a(value) {
    this.val = value;
  }
}
```

Examples of **correct** code for this rule:

```js
var o = {
  set a(value) {
    this.val = value;
  },
  get a() {
    return this.val;
  },
};

class C {
  set a(value) {
    this.val = value;
  }
  get a() {
    return this.val;
  }
}
```

## Configuration

